content.text:
Helper at `repack.cpp:1738-1751`, called at the **top of the block loop** in all 6 kernels.

## The call site

Always the first statement inside `for (int l = 0; l < nb; ++l)`, before any weight byte of block `l` is touched (`repack.cpp:1874-1877`):

```c
for (int l = 0; l < nb; ++l) {
    q1_prefetch_block(bx, l, nb);          // pull block l+1 into cache
    const vfloat32m2_t dx = q1_expand_fp16_64_m2(bx[l].d);
    const uint8_t * planes = (const uint8_t *) bx[l].qs;
    ...                                     // work on block l hides the miss
```

| line | kernel |
|---|---|
| `:1875` | `q1_gemv_64_vd4dot_vl1024` |
| `:1954` | `q1_gemm_64_vd4dot_vl1024` |
| `:2005` / `:2033` | plain-RVV gemv, VLEN 512 / 1024 |
| `:2069` / `:2112` | plain-RVV gemm, VLEN 512 / 1024 |

## The helper

```c
static inline __attribute__((always_inline))
void q1_prefetch_block(const block_q1_0x64 * bx, int l, int nb) {
    const int t = l + Q1_PREFETCH_DIST;
    if (t < nb) {
        const char * p = (const char *) &bx[t];
        for (size_t o = 0; o < sizeof(block_q1_0x64); o += 64) {
            __builtin_prefetch(p + o, 0, 3);
        }
    }
}
```

One `block_q1_0x64` is 1152 B = **18 cache lines**, so one call emits 18 `prefetch.r`. `Q1_PREFETCH_DIST` defaults to 1 (`:1736`): one block of lookahead measured best on `ax46mpv_fpga_l3` (2.14M -> 1.39M cycles on the K=51 V-proj node, 1.54x). Distances 2 and 4 were worse - one block ahead already hides the L3/DRAM latency, more only adds MSHR pressure.

## Two things that are load-bearing

**`always_inline` is not a hint.** A prefetch has no observable side effect, so whenever GCC leaves the helper out of line, `ipa-pure-const` marks it pure and DCE deletes every call. No warning, and results stay correct so no test notices. GCC 14.2 does exactly that at `-Os` (CMake `MinSizeRel`). `check-prefetch.sh` and `check-vd4dots.sh` count `prefetch.r` per kernel body to catch it - that is the `pf1` field in the gate output.

**`-march` needs `zicbop`**, else `__builtin_prefetch` compiles to nothing. `build.sh` passes `-DGGML_RV_ZICBOP=ON` for exactly this.

`Q1_PREFETCH_DIST=0` disables it entirely - that is what the `d4-nopf` / `baseline` build targets use for the A/B.
